// Sentura Enterprise Knowledge Graph (EKG) — 4-Pillar JSON5 Schema
//
// This file is the reference schema for structured enterprise knowledge stored
// in each agent's workspace `ekg/` directory. It is NOT loaded at runtime — it
// exists to document the agreed format for Data Scavenger output, industry
// ontology templates, and Experience Link extraction.
//
// See README.md §6 (Enterprise Knowledge Graph) for the architectural rationale.
//
// ============================================================================
// Directory Convention
// ============================================================================
//
// Each agent's workspace contains:
//
//   {workspace}/
//   └── ekg/
//       ├── org/                     # Pillar 1: Organization
//       │   ├── org-chart.json5
//       │   ├── departments.json5
//       │   ├── key-personnel.json5
//       │   └── approval-chains.json5
//       ├── rules/                   # Pillar 2: Rules & Policies
//       │   ├── financial-controls.json5
//       │   ├── data-handling.json5
//       │   ├── compliance.json5
//       │   └── escalation-policies.json5
//       ├── assets/                  # Pillar 3: Systems, Data, Tools
//       │   ├── systems.json5
//       │   ├── data-sources.json5
//       │   ├── mcp-servers.json5
//       │   └── credentials.json5    # references only; never secrets
//       └── workflows/               # Pillar 4: Procedures, SOPs, Experience
//           ├── procedures.json5
//           ├── sops.json5
//           ├── decision-trees.json5
//           └── experience-links/    # Tier 3 — autonomously extracted
//               └── *.json5
//
// Orchestrator (Manager) agents also have:
//   ekg/capabilities/{agent-id}.json5   # auto-extracted capability tags
//   ekg/conflicts/pending/*.json5       # awaiting human resolution
//   ekg/conflicts/resolved/*.json5      # resolved + Global SOP linked
//   ekg/insights/*.json5                # reverse-injection training directives
//   ekg/global-sops/*.json5             # cross-department standard SOPs
//
// ============================================================================
// Common Types (Referenced by All Pillars)
// ============================================================================
//
// Every top-level JSON5 file follows this envelope:
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     pillar: "org" | "rules" | "assets" | "workflows",
//     domain: "<sub-pillar>",           // e.g., "org-chart", "financial-controls"
//     entities: [ /* Entity[] */ ],
//     relations: [ /* Relation[] */ ],
//     provenance: { /* Provenance */ }, // file-level default provenance
//     lastUpdated: "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z",
//   }
//
// --- Entity ---------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Required: id, type, name
// Optional: attributes, tags, provenance (overrides file-level)
//
//   {
//     id: "entity:dept:finance",      // stable unique ID (slug-scoped)
//     type: "department",             // entity kind (pillar-specific vocab)
//     name: "Finance Department",
//     attributes: {
//       headcount: 12,
//       location: "HQ Floor 3",
//     },
//     tags: ["internal", "reporting-chain"],
//     provenance: {
//       source: "company-handbook.pdf",
//       ingested: "2026-04-15T14:22:00Z",
//       ingestedBy: "data-scavenger",
//       confidence: 0.92,
//     },
//   }
//
// --- Relation -------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Required: from, type, to
// Optional: attributes, provenance
//
//   {
//     from: "entity:person:cfo-jane",
//     type: "approves",                // relation verb (pillar-specific vocab)
//     to: "entity:action:payment-above-5k",
//     attributes: {
//       threshold: 5000,
//       currency: "USD",
//     },
//     provenance: {
//       source: "finance-policy-v3.pdf",
//       ingested: "2026-04-14T09:30:00Z",
//       ingestedBy: "data-scavenger",
//       confidence: 0.88,
//     },
//   }
//
// --- Provenance -----------------------------------------------------------
//
// Required: source, ingested
// Optional: ingestedBy, confidence, reviewedBy, reviewedAt, notes
//
//   {
//     source: "file:company-handbook.pdf" | "url:https://..." | "verbal:admin-jane" | "autonomous_extraction",
//     ingested: "ISO-8601 timestamp",
//     ingestedBy: "data-scavenger" | "creator" | "manual" | "experience-extractor",
//     confidence: 0.0..1.0,             // LLM classification confidence (0-1)
//     reviewedBy: "platform-admin@company.com",  // optional human review
//     reviewedAt: "ISO-8601",
//     notes: "Reviewed and verified correct",
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Pillar 1 — Organization (ekg/org/)
// ============================================================================
//
// Models the enterprise structure: departments, reporting lines, key personnel,
// approval chains, geographic locations, cost centers.
//
// Entity types:
//   - department        (team, unit, business group)
//   - person            (employees with decision authority)
//   - role              (titles: "CFO", "AP Clerk", "Compliance Officer")
//   - location          (office, region, country)
//   - cost-center       (budgetary grouping)
//   - external-party    (vendor, partner, regulator)
//
// Relation types:
//   - reports-to        (person -> person or role -> role)
//   - member-of         (person -> department)
//   - holds             (person -> role)
//   - approves          (person/role -> action entity in rules)
//   - located-at        (department -> location)
//   - owns-budget       (cost-center -> department)
//
// Example file: ekg/org/org-chart.json5
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     pillar: "org",
//     domain: "org-chart",
//     entities: [
//       { id: "entity:role:cfo", type: "role", name: "Chief Financial Officer" },
//       { id: "entity:role:controller", type: "role", name: "Controller" },
//       { id: "entity:role:ap-clerk", type: "role", name: "Accounts Payable Clerk" },
//       { id: "entity:person:jane-doe", type: "person", name: "Jane Doe", attributes: { email: "jane@co.com" } },
//     ],
//     relations: [
//       { from: "entity:role:ap-clerk", type: "reports-to", to: "entity:role:controller" },
//       { from: "entity:role:controller", type: "reports-to", to: "entity:role:cfo" },
//       { from: "entity:person:jane-doe", type: "holds", to: "entity:role:cfo" },
//     ],
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Pillar 2 — Rules & Policies (ekg/rules/)
// ============================================================================
//
// Models the hard constraints: financial approval thresholds, compliance
// requirements, data classification rules, escalation policies. Content in
// this pillar is cross-referenced by the `## Hard Rules (must not override)` section inside `AGENTS.md` for hard enforcement.
//
// Entity types:
//   - rule              (a single enforceable constraint)
//   - policy            (a group of related rules)
//   - threshold         (numeric limit: e.g., "$5,000")
//   - restricted-action (action requiring approval or prohibited outright)
//   - data-class        (T0-T4 classification)
//
// Relation types:
//   - governs           (policy -> action or person)
//   - requires-approval (action -> role/person)
//   - restricted-to     (action -> data-class)
//   - escalates-to      (rule -> role/person)
//   - supersedes        (rule -> rule)
//
// Example file: ekg/rules/financial-controls.json5
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     pillar: "rules",
//     domain: "financial-controls",
//     entities: [
//       {
//         id: "entity:rule:payment-approval-5k",
//         type: "rule",
//         name: "Payments above $5,000 require CFO approval",
//         attributes: { threshold: 5000, currency: "USD", severity: "hard" },
//       },
//       {
//         id: "entity:rule:duplicate-invoice-block",
//         type: "rule",
//         name: "Block duplicate invoices within 30 days",
//         attributes: { window_days: 30, severity: "hard" },
//       },
//     ],
//     relations: [
//       {
//         from: "entity:rule:payment-approval-5k",
//         type: "escalates-to",
//         to: "entity:role:cfo",
//       },
//     ],
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Pillar 3 — Assets (ekg/assets/)
// ============================================================================
//
// Models the tools, systems, data sources, and MCP servers available to the
// agent. This pillar is used to answer "what can this agent access?" and to
// wire up MCP server references during Creator Agent Phase 3.
//
// Entity types:
//   - system            (internal app: ERP, CRM, ticketing)
//   - data-source       (database, data warehouse, spreadsheet)
//   - mcp-server        (OpenClaw-registered MCP server)
//   - credential-ref    (secret store reference, NEVER the secret itself)
//   - api-endpoint      (external REST/GraphQL endpoint)
//   - document-repo     (knowledge base, SharePoint, Drive)
//
// Relation types:
//   - exposed-via       (system -> mcp-server)
//   - reads-from        (mcp-server -> data-source)
//   - authenticates-with (mcp-server -> credential-ref)
//   - belongs-to        (system -> department)
//
// Example file: ekg/assets/mcp-servers.json5
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     pillar: "assets",
//     domain: "mcp-servers",
//     entities: [
//       {
//         id: "entity:mcp:gradsale-admin",
//         type: "mcp-server",
//         name: "GradSale Admin API",
//         attributes: {
//           transport: "stdio",
//           command: "node",
//           args: ["sentura/mcp-servers/gradsale-admin/dist/index.js"],
//           scope: "admin",
//           dataClass: "T3",
//         },
//       },
//     ],
//     relations: [
//       {
//         from: "entity:mcp:gradsale-admin",
//         type: "authenticates-with",
//         to: "entity:credential-ref:gradsale_admin_token",
//       },
//     ],
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Pillar 4 — Workflows (ekg/workflows/)
// ============================================================================
//
// Models the procedural knowledge: SOPs, decision trees, standard workflows,
// and autonomously extracted Experience Links.
//
// Entity types:
//   - procedure         (a named multi-step process)
//   - step              (a single step in a procedure)
//   - decision-point    (a branch condition)
//   - outcome           (terminal state)
//   - experience-link   (pattern learned from observation — see Tier 3 below)
//
// Relation types:
//   - has-step          (procedure -> step)
//   - next              (step -> step, with optional condition attribute)
//   - branches-at       (procedure -> decision-point)
//   - results-in        (decision-point -> outcome, with `when` attribute)
//   - triggers          (outcome -> procedure)
//   - refines           (experience-link -> procedure)
//
// Example file: ekg/workflows/sops.json5
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     pillar: "workflows",
//     domain: "sops",
//     entities: [
//       {
//         id: "entity:procedure:ap-invoice-intake",
//         type: "procedure",
//         name: "Accounts Payable — Invoice Intake",
//         attributes: {
//           ownerRole: "ap-clerk",
//           averageDurationMinutes: 8,
//         },
//       },
//     ],
//     relations: [],
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Experience Link Format (Capability #13 — Tier 3)
// ============================================================================
//
// Experience Links are autonomously extracted patterns from the agent's task
// history. They are created by the `experience-extraction` skill during the
// dreaming cycle (deep phase) and promoted when confidence thresholds are met.
//
// File path: ekg/workflows/experience-links/{id}.json5
//
// Required fields: id, pattern, observation, confidence, occurrences,
//                  firstSeen, lastSeen, context, source
//
//   {
//     id: "exp:refund-under-50-auto-approve",
//     pattern: "When refund amount < $50 AND customer tier == 'premium', auto-approve without CFO escalation.",
//     observation: "Observed 23 cases where this flow completed without incident across 6 months.",
//     confidence: 0.87,           // decays over time unless reinforced
//     occurrences: 23,             // how many times this pattern was reinforced
//     firstSeen: "2025-10-12T14:20:00Z",
//     lastSeen: "2026-04-08T11:42:00Z",
//     context: {
//       role: "cs-agent",
//       department: "customer-support",
//       relatedRules: ["entity:rule:refund-approval-thresholds"],
//     },
//     source: "autonomous_extraction",
//     promotionStatus: "candidate" | "promoted" | "retired",
//     // Optional:
//     reviewedBy: "platform-admin@company.com",
//     reviewedAt: "2026-04-10T09:00:00Z",
//   }
//
// Promotion thresholds (defaults, configurable per agent):
//   - minOccurrences: 3
//   - minConfidence: 0.7
//   - minAgeHours: 48  (prevent promoting a burst of identical events)
//
// Confidence decay: 5% per 30 days without reinforcement, floor at 0.1.
//
// ============================================================================
// Manager Capability Tag Schema (Capability #17 — Mechanism 1)
// ============================================================================
//
// Stored on the Orchestrator at ekg/capabilities/{agent-id}.json5. Auto-written
// by Creator Agent Phase 5 (Deploy) when a new employee is incubated.
//
//   {
//     schemaVersion: "1.0",
//     agentId: "cs-agent-gradsale",
//     capabilities: [
//       { tag: "dispute-resolution", description: "Resolve e-commerce buyer-seller disputes" },
//       { tag: "refund-processing", description: "Process customer refunds up to $500" },
//     ],
//     inputSchema: {
//       required: ["disputeId"],
//       optional: ["priority", "customerTier"],
//     },
//     outputSchema: {
//       produces: ["resolution", "refundAmount", "auditNote"],
//     },
//     lastUpdated: "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z",
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Cross-Domain Conflict Resolution Protocol (Capability #17 — Mechanism 2)
// ============================================================================
//
// Conflict entries are created by the Orchestrator's cross-domain conflict
// detection skill. Pending conflicts require human resolution via the approval
// system. Resolved conflicts produce a Global SOP.
//
// Path: ekg/conflicts/pending/{id}.json5
//
//   {
//     id: "conflict:2026-04-16-refund-vs-revenue-rec",
//     detectedAt: "2026-04-16T10:15:00Z",
//     departments: ["customer-support", "finance"],
//     description: "Customer Support auto-refunds under $50; Finance requires CFO sign-off on any refund after month-end close.",
//     conflicting_rules: [
//       { agentId: "cs-agent", rule: "entity:rule:auto-refund-under-50" },
//       { agentId: "ap-clerk", rule: "entity:rule:post-close-refund-approval" },
//     ],
//     severity: "medium",           // low | medium | high
//     proposedResolution: "Post-close auto-refunds capped at $25; remainder escalates to CFO.",
//     escalatedTo: "entity:role:cfo",
//   }
//
// After resolution (moved to ekg/conflicts/resolved/):
//   {
//     ...original fields...,
//     resolvedBy: "platform-admin@company.com",
//     resolvedAt: "2026-04-17T14:22:00Z",
//     globalSopRef: "entity:procedure:post-close-refund-handling",
//   }
//
// ============================================================================
// Industry Ontology Template Format
// ============================================================================
//
// Industry ontology templates live at:
//   sentura/config/industry-ontologies/{industry}/
//
// The directory structure mirrors the agent `ekg/` layout (org/, rules/,
// assets/, workflows/). Each file follows the pillar schema above.
//
// Template files use `{placeholder}` convention for values that are customized
// at incubation time (e.g., `{company_name}`, `{compliance_contact}`).
//
// Creator Agent Phase 2 merges the selected industry ontology into the new
// agent's `ekg/` directory, preserving any existing files (additive merge).
//
// ============================================================================
// Merge Semantics
// ============================================================================
//
// 1. Additive only — NEVER delete existing entities or relations.
// 2. Entity deduplication — match on `id`. If same id exists with different
//    attributes, the newer provenance wins, but all sources are recorded in
//    `provenance.previousSources: [...]`.
//
// 3. Relation deduplication — match on `from + type + to` tuple. Duplicates
//    are collapsed; attributes are merged (newer wins on conflict).
//
// 4. Low-confidence items (confidence < 0.5) are flagged for human review and
//    stored in a sibling `_review/` subdirectory until reviewed.
//
// ============================================================================
// File Size & Splitting
// ============================================================================
//
// Any single JSON5 file that exceeds 256 KB should be split by sub-domain:
//   org/org-chart.json5           -> org/org-chart-sales.json5, org/org-chart-eng.json5
//
// The `sentura-bootstrap` hook scans the full `ekg/` tree regardless of file
// count; splitting improves git diff readability and hot-reload performance.
